NAME
       pipe - create a pipe

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int pipe(int fd[2]);

DESCRIPTION
       Creates a one-way channel. FD[0] is the read end and FD[1] the
       write end. Data written to one comes out of the other in order.

       A read blocks while the pipe is empty and some writer still has
       the write end open; once every writer has closed it, the read
       returns 0. Writing to a pipe with no reader raises SIGPIPE.

       Each end should be closed in the process that does not use it,
       or the end-of-file will never arrive.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EMFILE  no free descriptors
       EFAULT  fd points outside the address space

SEE ALSO
       dup(2), poll(2), fork(2)
